Track 3: The Accelerator Shift Blues
- Story & Context: Legend holds that this track was recorded in a single unedited take during the final night before the city sealed the accelerator tunnel's main intake shaft. The local crowd lined the curved wall in total silence, holding up pocket lighters as the bagpipes and sliding 808s achieved a resonant acoustic standing wave that made the concrete dust dance off the floor. Today, the song operates as the scene’s unofficial national anthem, played at the end of every underground subterranean set across the city. "They welded up the door but they left the hum, long after winter and the train don't come."
